      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Different teams were using these different attributes (Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant, Payments Ops used department=payments), causing the ingestion normalization to fail collapsing them into a single canonical attribute, which led to the Rules Engine failing to match entity tags for routing approvals. Jin proposed a fast fix that involved adding a preprocessing mapping rule in Signal Ingest to map businessUnit to department (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change, hot-reloadable, and does not require any appliance restart or waiting on Okta change control, enabling a quick remediation without the 2\u20134 week delay of standardizing at the identity source (Okta) [art_79f625aafa16, art_e60697c15fce].",
