      "answer": "Among the North America West Event Nexus accounts, the following customers are dealing with taxonomy/search semantics problems:\n\n- Arcadia Cloudworks: search relevance degradation after taxonomy v2.1 rollout causing missing or low-ranked results and playbook trigger misses (~28%) [art_90991e25335f].\n- BlueHarbor Logistics: search relevance degraded after taxonomy rollout on 2026-02-20, with poor and duplicate results increasing manual triage; root cause includes schema registry version mismatch and index weighting issues [art_8b0063fbb3cb, art_bd3560dfe194].\n- CedarWind Renewables: search relevance fell from ~68% to ~32% after taxonomy update; queries return unrelated incidents, increasing manual triage [art_10f7e8b72e09].\n- HelioFab Systems: taxonomy refactor caused missed dedupe matches and irrelevant search results, affecting runbook trigger accuracy [art_9345d5653840].\n- Pacific Health Network: search relevance dropped after taxonomy update on 2026-03-02; incidents grouped incorrectly and playbooks misfiring [art_4eccfd9dcf29].\n- Pioneer Freight Solutions: low-relevance matches and notionally identical incidents not grouped after taxonomy update; suspected schema version mismatch [art_3ba29fe1e026].\n\nRegarding duplicate-action problems, the evidence does not explicitly identify any North America West Event Nexus accounts primarily dealing with duplicate-action issues. One support ticket mentions role provisioning lag and duplicative accounts after a February 2026 org restructure, but it is not linked to Event Nexus or taxonomy/search semantics and does not specify a North America West Event Nexus customer [art_d11447325b44].\n\nTherefore, all the listed North America West Event Nexus accounts are primarily facing taxonomy/search semantics problems rather than duplicate-action problems. No accounts in the evidence are identified as primarily dealing with duplicate-action problems.",
